.. == 13 else 10`, src/gnd/redaction.py:732). A refusal gate keyed to the stated {10,13} version set would miss temporal-model outputs, which land on version 11.\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Correct the citation to name all projected versions (9->10/13 redaction, 11 temporal) or, better, phrase RC1 D3's refusal in terms of model properties (active redaction policy, temporal terms) rather than wire versions, and pin the corrected fact in the RC1 spec.\",\"relevance\":\"hardening\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"title\":\"Re-projection version claim in RC1 omits the temporal v11 arm\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"rca-r2-02\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/rule-check-adoption/notes/rule-check-adoption-plan.md\",\"location\":\"§4 RC2-C4 (line 225) and RC3-C5 (line 236)\",\"observation\":\"RC2-C4 reads \\\"time bound over 2,000+ edges\\\" and RC3-C5 reads \\\"time bound over 2,000+ rows\\\". No numeric bound is stated anywhere in the plan, so a run of the stated work could not fail either criterion — any runtime satisfies it. Every other named criterion (e.g. RC1-C3 byte equality, RC3-C4 insertion stability) has a concrete falsifiable form; these two do not, despite the plan presenting them as named phase criteria and the rubric requiring falsifiability.\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Pin a numeric budget in each criterion (or explicitly defer the number to the spec with a requirement that the spec state one), e.g. derived from the O15 observation of 2.5 s for 2,047 edges, which the plan already records — marked as a claim, not reproduced.\",\"relevance\":\"hardening\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"title\":\"Time-bound criteria are not falsifiable as written\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"rca-r2-03\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/rule-check-adoption/notes/rule-check-adoption-plan.md\",\"location\":\"§3 artifact homes table, line 200\",\"observation\":\"The table assigns the declared address to \\\"`src/gnd/address.py` (`declared_constraint_address`,